.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH snp 1  "snp 2.0.0" 
.SH NAME
snp \- You Shell Not Pass: a fast, drop\-in pre\-commit runner
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBsnp\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] [\fIsubcommands\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
You Shell Not Pass: a fast, drop\-in pre\-commit runner
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
show this help message and exit
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
show program\*(Aqs version number and exit
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
snp\-autoupdate(1)
Auto\-update snp config to the latest repos\*(Aq versions.
.TP
snp\-cache(1)
Inspect or clean snp\*(Aqs cache.
.TP
snp\-clean(1)
Clean out snp files.
.TP
snp\-completions(1)
Print a shell completion script.
.TP
snp\-config(1)
Print the merged configuration or its JSON schema.
.TP
snp\-doctor(1)
Check snp, the hook scripts and the cache for problems.
.TP
snp\-gc(1)
Clean unused cached repos.
.TP
snp\-hazmat(1)
Composable tools for rare use in hook `entry`.
.TP
snp\-init\-templatedir(1)
Install hook script in a directory intended for use with `git config init.templateDir`.
.TP
snp\-install(1)
Install the snp script.
.TP
snp\-install\-hooks(1)
Install hook environments for all environments in the config file.  You may find `snp install \-\-install\-hooks` more useful.
.TP
snp\-list(1)
List the hooks of the configuration.
.TP
snp\-migrate(1)
Convert lefthook configurations or switch pre\-commit\-hooks to and from `repo: builtin`.
.TP
snp\-migrate\-config(1)
Migrate list configuration to new map configuration.
.TP
snp\-run(1)
Run hooks.
.TP
snp\-sample\-config(1)
Produce a sample .pre\-commit\-config.yaml file
.TP
snp\-self(1)
Manage the snp installation.
.TP
snp\-try\-repo(1)
Try the hooks in a repository, useful for developing new hooks.
.TP
snp\-uninstall(1)
Uninstall the snp script.
.TP
snp\-validate\-config(1)
Validate .pre\-commit\-config.yaml files
.TP
snp\-validate\-manifest(1)
Validate .pre\-commit\-hooks.yaml files
.TP
snp\-help(1)
Show help for a specific command.
.SH VERSION
v2.0.0
